## Proposed B1 policy from issue #287

For main as the staging gate, require a combined score of at least 95, every facet at ordinal 85 or higher, and no facet below 60. Keep P10's program-exit gate at the current full 95/95/95 bar. Keep hard gates and the all-facet ratchet binding.

## Decisions required before implementation

The proposed wording needs Lucas's clarification before any threshold code can change:

1. The current translation ordinal is 60. A literal requirement that every facet be at least 85 still fails this report; the separate 60 floor would be redundant. Confirm whether 85 is mandatory for every staging facet or whether 60 is the absolute staging floor, with 85 as a target that triggers investigation.
2. The current main gate also requires every facet's Jev confidence to be at least 0.95. B1 does not state whether this confidence requirement changes for staging. Confirm the staging confidence rule explicitly.
3. Confirm that B1 applies only to merged main as staging, with the full 95/95/95 program-exit rule retained for P10 and scoped PR reports remaining advisory under A-005.

Only after written approval should the agreed text be appended as the next approved amendment, the hash chain be rebuilt, and the corresponding staging-gate code and tests be changed. No threshold change is included in this draft.
